WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.836
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.106 --> 00:03.442
[♪ theme song playing]

3
00:03.525 --> 00:04.651
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

4
00:04.735 --> 00:06.028
START DATING...

5
00:36.725 --> 00:41.063
BETWEEN STEPS

6
00:41.730 --> 00:43.940
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:44.024 --> 00:45.609
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

8
00:47.110 --> 00:49.321
EPISODE 7

9
00:51.156 --> 00:54.159
[♪ classical music playing over speakers]

10
00:56.328 --> 00:58.580
-Subin, would you like some fried rice? -Yeah.

11
00:59.998 --> 01:01.500
-[Youjin] This much? -Yeah.

12
01:07.297 --> 01:08.465
-You want salmon? -Yeah.

13
01:08.548 --> 01:10.384
-Salmon's nice. -I'm going to have some.

14
01:10.467 --> 01:11.927
[Youjin] I'll take the squid.

15
01:13.261 --> 01:15.055
-Do you want some salmon? -Just a piece.

16
01:23.397 --> 01:24.648
[in English] Thank you.

17
01:26.441 --> 01:27.776
[in Korean] Hello. [chuckles]

18
01:39.121 --> 01:40.706
-Enjoy. -Thanks.

19
01:41.206 --> 01:42.207
Enjoy, everyone.

20
01:42.833 --> 01:44.918
Here, help yourself.

21
01:45.001 --> 01:46.503
-Thank you. -Sure.

22
01:47.045 --> 01:48.463
Just relax and enjoy your food.

23
01:48.547 --> 01:49.798
[both chuckle]

24
01:53.301 --> 01:54.594
-You know what? -Yeah?

25
01:54.678 --> 01:56.388
-I'll treat you next time. -Nah.

26
01:57.222 --> 01:59.766
There's a new place near campus that has amazing tiramisu.

27
01:59.850 --> 02:01.810
Tiramishu? I love tiramishu.

28
02:02.310 --> 02:03.353
[Chansoo] "Tiramishu?"

29
02:03.437 --> 02:05.355
What's that? Is it something tasty?

30
02:06.148 --> 02:08.483
Tiramishu is a kind of pastry.

31
02:09.359 --> 02:11.361
Didn't you know that?

32
02:11.445 --> 02:13.822
It's not a pastry. It's a cake. [chuckles nervously]

33
02:14.948 --> 02:17.868
So, to be precise,

34
02:17.951 --> 02:20.120
it's not "tiramishu."

35
02:20.203 --> 02:22.664
It's "su." [chuckles]

36
02:22.748 --> 02:24.708
It's Italian, "tiramisu."

37
02:24.791 --> 02:25.792
Oh.

38
02:26.209 --> 02:29.087
You see, it's a traditional Italian cake.

39
02:29.171 --> 02:31.631
You know, in Italiano.

40
02:32.132 --> 02:33.133
"Tiramisu."

41
02:34.843 --> 02:35.844
Oh...

42
02:35.927 --> 02:37.429
[chuckling] It's nothing.

43
02:38.180 --> 02:42.559
So, Subin, you like tiramisu?

44
02:42.642 --> 02:43.810
I love it too.

45
02:43.894 --> 02:45.771
-Yes. -[Subin chuckles awkwardly]

46
02:45.854 --> 02:48.857
Actually, since we're on the subject,

47
02:48.940 --> 02:50.901
why don't we go try it today? Are you free?

48
02:52.194 --> 02:54.196
I don't think I can today.

49
02:54.279 --> 02:56.156
I need to get back to work.

50
02:57.491 --> 02:59.785
You're busy even on the weekend, huh?

51
02:59.868 --> 03:01.912
What time will you be done?

52
03:01.995 --> 03:04.790
Let's go when you're done. What time do you finish?

53
03:04.873 --> 03:07.793
Ah. I'm not sure yet.

54
03:07.876 --> 03:08.877
[Taeho] I see.

55
03:09.377 --> 03:10.712
[Subin clears throat]

56
03:16.051 --> 03:17.052
[Minjae] Hmm?

57
03:17.511 --> 03:19.805
-Where did you get the orange juice? -This?

58
03:19.888 --> 03:22.516
Next to the soda fountain. Should I get you some?

59
03:23.475 --> 03:24.476
I'll go get it myself.

60
03:25.393 --> 03:26.394
No, I can go get it.

61
03:26.478 --> 03:28.563
-Subin, do you want some juice too? -Yeah, sure.

62
03:28.647 --> 03:31.024
-[Minjae] I'll get you some. -[Hangyeol] Don't. I'll go get it.

63
03:31.858 --> 03:33.568
-I'll go get it. -No, I'll go get it.

64
03:33.652 --> 03:35.779
-I can go get it. -What? No, I'll go get it.

65
03:35.862 --> 03:37.155
Come on, don't be like that.

66
03:37.239 --> 03:38.281
What are you doing?

67
03:38.365 --> 03:39.449
I can go get it myself.

68
03:39.533 --> 03:40.534
[Hangyeol] No.

69
03:44.454 --> 03:47.123
My lab mates are all really nice.

70
03:47.207 --> 03:48.208
Oh.

71
03:48.291 --> 03:50.544
-Yeah. -They're all really nice.

72
03:51.127 --> 03:52.212
Oh...

73
03:52.295 --> 03:55.840
Ah. Minjae, I wonder if she's at the airport by now.

74
03:56.424 --> 03:58.218
I think so. She must have.

75
03:58.802 --> 04:01.346
Right, why did they change their honeymoon from Hawaii to Phuket?

76
04:01.429 --> 04:03.557
They both work full-time. They don't have time.

77
04:04.057 --> 04:06.893
Still, you only get to go on your honeymoon once.

78
04:07.936 --> 04:09.729
-Here. Orange juice. -Oh!

79
04:09.813 --> 04:11.314
-Thank you. -[chuckles]

80
04:15.110 --> 04:16.361
Thank you. Let me...

81
04:17.487 --> 04:18.905
-It's grape juice. -Oh.

82
04:19.906 --> 04:20.907
Ah...

83
04:20.991 --> 04:22.659
Okay. Thank you.

84
04:23.743 --> 04:25.078
[Sejin coughs]

85
04:26.329 --> 04:27.706
-Which one do you want? -[Minjae] Here.

86
04:27.789 --> 04:29.541
-I... -[Minjae] Drink this. Here.

87
04:31.251 --> 04:33.169
-No, I'm fine. -[Youjin] You can have both.

88
04:33.253 --> 04:35.755
-No, I'm fine. -No, you should drink it.

89
04:38.592 --> 04:40.427
-Huh? -[phone vibrating]

90
04:40.510 --> 04:41.761
I'll be right back.

91
04:42.596 --> 04:43.722
Yes, Professor.

92
04:45.849 --> 04:47.851
-[Sejin coughing] -Yes.

93
04:47.934 --> 04:50.228
I just stepped out to grab a bite.

94
04:51.354 --> 04:52.355
-Yes. -What's up?

95
04:52.439 --> 04:54.107
Okay, I will. Bye.

96
04:55.942 --> 04:57.694
I'm sorry, but I need to head out now.

97
04:58.320 --> 04:59.362
[Youjin] Okay, bye.

98
04:59.446 --> 05:00.447
-[Subin] Sorry. -But...

99
05:00.530 --> 05:01.531
-Take care. -But...

100
05:02.490 --> 05:05.285
-Wait. -Well, I'll see you next time. I'm sorry.

101
05:05.368 --> 05:07.037
-[Chansoo] Wait... -[Hangyeol] What time do you get off?

102
05:07.871 --> 05:08.955
What time do you...

103
05:09.581 --> 05:10.999
[Youjin] Come on, for God's sake.

104
05:15.670 --> 05:18.423
Hey, since it's the weekend and we're all here,

105
05:18.506 --> 05:21.635
how about we go grab a beer or something? What do you say?

106
05:21.718 --> 05:22.719
-Then... -Yeah?

107
05:22.802 --> 05:25.388
There's this new dessert place that has amazing tiramisu.

108
05:25.472 --> 05:26.932
Hmm.

109
05:27.015 --> 05:28.808
Then, shall we go get some coffee and cake?

110
05:28.892 --> 05:30.685
Hold on a second. [grunts]

111
05:32.187 --> 05:34.356
I wonder if the baseball game has begun.

112
05:34.439 --> 05:35.523
I'll watch the game, then.

113
05:35.607 --> 05:37.817
Yeah. Hey, put it on. It has already started.

114
05:38.485 --> 05:39.653
I'll just watch the game.

115
05:40.236 --> 05:42.197
-[Chansoo] All right. -[Taeho] Okay.

116
05:42.280 --> 05:44.658
-You... You good? All right. -[Sejin] Yes?

117
05:46.117 --> 05:47.911
[camera shutter clicking]

118
05:47.994 --> 05:49.162
Look here.

119
05:49.245 --> 05:51.456
-Don't take my picture. [chuckles] -Come on.

120
05:51.539 --> 05:52.958
Could you turn your head a little bit?

121
05:53.500 --> 05:55.919
-No, I don't want to. -But you look great on camera.

122
05:56.002 --> 05:57.003
Okay, fine.

123
06:01.257 --> 06:02.258
You took it, right?

124
06:03.426 --> 06:04.719
Now, I'll try this.

125
06:10.350 --> 06:11.685
Mmm!

126
06:11.768 --> 06:12.769
It's good.

127
06:12.852 --> 06:14.270
-It's good, right? -Mmm.

128
06:14.354 --> 06:15.397
Try this too.

129
06:15.480 --> 06:17.023
Okay. Sejin, do you want to try?

130
06:17.524 --> 06:19.484
No, I don't have a sweet tooth.

131
06:19.567 --> 06:20.568
[Minjae] You don't?

132
06:21.403 --> 06:23.405
If so, why did you follow us here?

133
06:24.739 --> 06:27.367
No, it's actually not as sweet as you think. Try it.

134
06:28.368 --> 06:29.369
Come on, try it.

135
06:29.452 --> 06:30.870
[indistinct laughter]

136
06:33.498 --> 06:34.708
Mmm.

137
06:34.791 --> 06:36.584
It's not bad. It's delicious.

138
06:39.754 --> 06:40.755
[sighs]

139
06:41.881 --> 06:44.217
How about we go to the movies? It's been a while.

140
06:44.718 --> 06:45.927
Anything you've been wanting to see?

141
06:46.720 --> 06:47.846
[Youjin] Hmm...

142
06:47.929 --> 06:49.305
I'm okay with anything.

143
06:49.806 --> 06:51.599
What should we see?

144
06:51.683 --> 06:53.935
It's the weekend, so there may be no tickets left.

145
06:54.018 --> 06:56.604
-Let me look it up. -Yeah, look it up.

146
06:58.982 --> 07:01.526
Action or adventure? What do you think?

147
07:01.609 --> 07:03.278
That looks good. Something light.

148
07:04.487 --> 07:07.615
How about this? I heard it's really fun. It's got good ratings too.

149
07:08.158 --> 07:10.535
I don't really like the poster. Is there anything else?

150
07:10.618 --> 07:12.579
Then, are you more into this kind of thing?

151
07:12.662 --> 07:15.582
That's a little... It's an animated movie.

152
07:16.082 --> 07:17.500
I should get going.

153
07:17.584 --> 07:19.127
I need to go home.

154
07:19.961 --> 07:20.962
Huh?

155
07:21.045 --> 07:22.046
You're not watching the movie?

156
07:22.589 --> 07:24.424
No, I think I should hurry back home.

157
07:24.924 --> 07:26.843
-Why? -Should I just buy two tickets, then?

158
07:26.926 --> 07:28.678
Yeah, buy two. Just for you and Minjae.

159
07:28.762 --> 07:31.222
-Okay. Two tickets. -No, wait. Wait, Youjin.

160
07:32.223 --> 07:33.224
I'll get the tickets, then.

161
07:45.904 --> 07:48.239
[muttering] Her and her damn temper...

162
07:53.411 --> 07:54.913
I'll be waiting outside.

163
07:54.996 --> 07:57.332
Hey, go tell Youjin to wait out front for a minute.

164
08:03.379 --> 08:05.423
Sejin, where's Youjin?

165
08:06.800 --> 08:08.259
She said she's going home and then left.

166
08:09.010 --> 08:10.011
She went home?

167
08:11.638 --> 08:13.306
-There's Lim Youjin. -Where?

168
08:13.890 --> 08:15.642
-The bus. On the bus. -On the bus? On it?

169
08:16.392 --> 08:17.393
I don't see her.

170
08:19.437 --> 08:21.523
-Now, she's really gone. -Jeez.

171
08:23.316 --> 08:24.818
That rude brat.

172
08:24.901 --> 08:27.237
I waved goodbye to her, and she gave me the finger.

173
08:50.093 --> 08:52.095
What should we have for dinner after the movie?

174
08:53.221 --> 08:54.222
Korean?

175
08:54.806 --> 08:55.807
Chinese?

176
08:56.307 --> 08:58.226
Japanese? Western?

177
08:58.810 --> 08:59.811
What would you like?

178
09:01.938 --> 09:03.648
Sejin, I'm really sorry.

179
09:05.859 --> 09:07.527
But can we see the movie another time?

180
09:10.238 --> 09:13.074
Well, I've been running around all day for the wedding, and...

181
09:14.534 --> 09:15.535
I'm a little tired.

182
09:20.957 --> 09:21.958
Minjae.

183
09:24.043 --> 09:25.545
Is your leg bothering you that much?

184
09:27.505 --> 09:28.840
No, it's just...

185
09:29.966 --> 09:31.050
[Sejin sighs]

186
09:31.926 --> 09:33.136
Let's see it another time.

187
09:35.805 --> 09:36.806
[phone vibrating]

188
09:45.940 --> 09:47.400
[Minjae] Did you get home okay?

189
09:51.905 --> 09:53.323
[quietly] Why isn't she replying?

190
09:57.243 --> 09:58.244
[sighs]

191
10:00.830 --> 10:01.831
[sighing]

192
10:10.882 --> 10:13.009
[long sigh]

193
10:13.092 --> 10:14.093
[hums]

194
10:18.139 --> 10:19.349
-[phone vibrating] -Mmm?

195
10:20.308 --> 10:23.311
-[♪ light music playing] -[phone vibrating]

196
10:31.611 --> 10:32.612
Hello?

197
10:33.196 --> 10:34.864
What took you so long to pick up?

198
10:36.658 --> 10:38.159
You're brushing your teeth?

199
10:38.701 --> 10:40.411
Should we talk later, then?

200
10:40.495 --> 10:44.874
No, I can talk now. I can talk. I'm done.

201
10:49.295 --> 10:50.296
Did I see the movie?

202
10:52.590 --> 10:54.217
No, I didn't see the movie.

203
10:55.301 --> 10:57.512
Why would I watch a movie with Kim Sejin?

204
10:58.137 --> 10:59.764
That's why I just came home.

205
11:00.390 --> 11:01.391
I'm home now.

206
11:02.225 --> 11:03.226
I mean...

207
11:03.851 --> 11:06.813
You and Kim Sejin even bought tickets. Why didn't you go?

208
11:07.313 --> 11:09.107
It sounded like a really fun movie.

209
11:09.190 --> 11:10.191
No, that was...

210
11:12.277 --> 11:15.113
He doesn't have any friends in Seoul,

211
11:15.947 --> 11:19.784
and the only people he knows are us from the lab.

212
11:20.702 --> 11:22.829
We should at least look out for him.

213
11:23.997 --> 11:27.417
And since you guys are in the same cohort, you should be nice to him too.

214
11:28.209 --> 11:31.254
Does Sejin really bother you that much?

215
11:31.337 --> 11:32.964
Do you get mad just looking at him?

216
11:33.047 --> 11:35.049
Well, it wasn't Kim Sejin...

217
11:36.426 --> 11:39.721
I wasn't mad at Kim Sejin. I was mad at Park Minjae.

218
11:40.638 --> 11:42.223
Me? Why?

219
11:43.224 --> 11:45.351
I don't think you like me that much.

220
11:50.690 --> 11:51.691
Are you still there?

221
11:52.233 --> 11:53.234
Yeah.

222
11:53.735 --> 11:54.736
I'm here.

223
11:56.362 --> 11:59.699
You like me way less than I like you.

224
12:01.075 --> 12:02.285
Be honest with me.

225
12:03.995 --> 12:08.082
If Kim Sejin and I were both drowning, who would you save first?

226
12:08.166 --> 12:09.167
What?

227
12:10.626 --> 12:11.836
[Youjin] Why won't you answer?

228
12:12.795 --> 12:14.630
Who would you save, Kim Sejin or me?

229
12:14.714 --> 12:15.757
[scoffs]

230
12:17.633 --> 12:20.178
That's just ridiculous. I don't even know what to say.

231
12:21.554 --> 12:23.014
[Youjin] Why is it ridiculous?

232
12:23.097 --> 12:24.766
I'm being totally serious.

233
12:27.185 --> 12:29.479
Well, of course...

234
12:31.230 --> 12:32.607
I'd save you.

235
12:34.692 --> 12:37.945
Even if we both fell in,

236
12:38.946 --> 12:41.741
I'd be begging, "Please save Youjin first."

237
12:45.036 --> 12:46.287
Did you hear what I said?

238
12:46.871 --> 12:48.373
Yeah, I'm listening.

239
12:50.708 --> 12:51.959
Then what if...

240
12:53.211 --> 12:57.423
our parents didn't approve of us being together? What would you do, then?

241
13:01.969 --> 13:03.304
Hello? Are you there?

242
13:04.722 --> 13:05.723
[Minjae] Yeah.

243
13:08.059 --> 13:09.769
What would you do?

244
13:11.187 --> 13:12.688
[Youjin] Well, I asked you first.

245
13:13.398 --> 13:15.274
What would you do if they didn't approve?

246
13:15.983 --> 13:16.984
Well...

247
13:20.530 --> 13:23.825
Well, it's not like we're still minors.

248
13:28.955 --> 13:32.291
We don't have to do everything our parents say, right?

249
13:32.375 --> 13:36.087
I think we can keep seeing each other even if they disapprove.

250
13:36.879 --> 13:37.880
Hmm.

251
13:39.090 --> 13:40.716
[Minjae] And what would you do?

252
13:41.676 --> 13:43.052
If our parents disapproved?

253
13:44.053 --> 13:47.056
[Youjin clears throat] Well, if your mom is against it,

254
13:47.140 --> 13:48.933
I think you should stop seeing that person.

255
13:49.684 --> 13:52.520
Who could possibly be more important than your mom?

256
13:52.603 --> 13:56.149
She gave birth to you and raised you, so she must have a good reason.

257
13:57.108 --> 13:58.693
I'd stop seeing you if my mom said so.

258
14:00.027 --> 14:01.279
[♪ soft music playing]

259
14:01.362 --> 14:02.363
Are you listening?

260
14:05.867 --> 14:08.494
Why does the connection keep cutting out?

261
14:12.081 --> 14:13.082
Oh.

262
14:15.334 --> 14:17.295
It must be because my battery is low.

263
14:20.214 --> 14:21.924
I've got to go now.

264
14:25.720 --> 14:26.721
Yeah.

265
14:27.555 --> 14:28.556
Okay.

266
14:29.265 --> 14:30.266
Bye.

267
14:36.272 --> 14:37.356
[line disconnects]

268
14:55.333 --> 14:57.335
[door opens]

269
14:58.461 --> 14:59.629
[door closes]

270
15:14.101 --> 15:15.102
Are you asleep?

271
15:17.939 --> 15:18.940
Hey, are you asleep?

272
15:20.566 --> 15:23.194
Sejin, hey, wake up. Go sleep at your place.

273
15:23.277 --> 15:24.654
-Huh? -[Sejin groans]

274
15:25.571 --> 15:27.490
-You should go home. -[Sejin] Ten more minutes.

275
15:28.241 --> 15:30.534
-What? -[muttering] Ten more minutes...

276
15:31.869 --> 15:32.870
Ten...

277
15:48.052 --> 15:49.345
[quietly] Here, cover up.

278
16:10.658 --> 16:11.951
[Minjae yelling] Jesus Christ!

279
16:12.034 --> 16:14.078
Hey, you punk, get out of my bed!

280
16:14.662 --> 16:15.788
I said get out of my bed!

281
16:15.871 --> 16:16.914
[Sejin groans]

282
16:18.499 --> 16:19.834
For God's sake.

283
16:23.296 --> 16:24.297
Gosh.

284
16:24.797 --> 16:26.841
I must've done it in my sleep.

285
16:28.092 --> 16:30.970
I didn't even realize it. I was freezing.

286
16:31.053 --> 16:32.054
Fine.

287
16:34.724 --> 16:39.520
Come on, it was just between us guys. You don't have to get so upset about it.

288
16:50.156 --> 16:52.658
Hey, there are plenty of empty seats over there.

289
16:52.742 --> 16:54.201
-Let's sit together. -Come on.

290
16:54.285 --> 16:55.661
[Subin] Hello.

291
16:56.579 --> 16:57.580
[Minjae] Hello.

292
16:58.164 --> 17:00.458
-Are you on your way to work? -[Subin] Yes.

293
17:01.083 --> 17:02.084
Hello.

294
17:03.377 --> 17:04.378
Hello.

295
17:10.343 --> 17:12.345
BUS COLLEGE OF ENGINEERING

296
17:27.360 --> 17:28.361
What are you doing?

297
17:31.030 --> 17:32.823
-Aren't you coming? -Yeah.

298
17:34.950 --> 17:37.161
Did you forget something? What were you staring at?

299
17:38.120 --> 17:39.372
I was just...

300
17:40.206 --> 17:43.125
checking to make sure the bus was running okay.

301
17:43.209 --> 17:44.585
What are you saying?

302
17:46.879 --> 17:49.256
-Wait, do you... -No.

303
17:49.882 --> 17:51.717
-You... [laughs] -I don't like her.

304
17:51.801 --> 17:52.802
Jeez.

305
17:54.720 --> 17:57.139
I don't. I don't!

306
17:57.973 --> 17:59.433
They say birds of a feather flock together.

307
18:00.059 --> 18:02.561
I can't believe she's Lim Youjin's friend.

308
18:02.645 --> 18:06.357
She may seem normal, but I'm sure she'll turn out weird too.

309
18:06.440 --> 18:08.192
Come on. That can't be true.

310
18:09.443 --> 18:13.656
Also, Youjin can be a little quirky and stubborn,

311
18:14.198 --> 18:16.033
but she's not weird or anything.

312
18:16.617 --> 18:17.702
She is.

313
18:17.785 --> 18:19.912
In fact, she's super weird.

314
18:20.496 --> 18:24.291
Okay, well... Enough about Youjin. What else is bothering you?

315
18:26.711 --> 18:27.712
Her face.

316
18:29.338 --> 18:30.339
She's...

317
18:31.132 --> 18:33.259
Isn't she ridiculously pretty?

318
18:33.342 --> 18:34.468
What?

319
18:35.970 --> 18:39.598
I mean, she's almost unrealistically beautiful.

320
18:39.682 --> 18:41.225
She doesn't even look like a real person.

321
18:41.809 --> 18:44.937
You almost start wondering if she's a fairy or an angel.

322
18:45.813 --> 18:48.983
So she looks like a fairy or an angel to you.

323
18:49.650 --> 18:51.861
Well, she's almost too beautiful, you know?

324
18:52.820 --> 18:56.115
She's crossed the line.

325
18:58.617 --> 18:59.827
[laughing] Okay, I get it.

326
19:00.453 --> 19:02.413
So, what else is bothering you?

327
19:02.496 --> 19:06.333
It doesn't make sense that someone like her is still single.

328
19:06.417 --> 19:10.671
She can basically date whoever she wants. So why doesn't she have a boyfriend yet?

329
19:10.755 --> 19:13.132
Maybe she just hasn't met the right person yet.

330
19:13.215 --> 19:14.508
That's a different matter.

331
19:14.592 --> 19:15.593
The right person...

332
19:18.179 --> 19:20.556
Am I the one she hasn't met yet?

333
19:20.639 --> 19:21.807
Do you think so too?

334
19:23.267 --> 19:24.810
Well, I don't know that.

335
19:25.394 --> 19:26.979
So why do you keep asking those questions?

336
19:27.938 --> 19:28.939
Well, I didn't.

337
19:30.816 --> 19:33.194
You brought it up first.

338
19:34.779 --> 19:36.489
[long sigh]

339
19:38.866 --> 19:39.992
Oh boy.

340
19:40.075 --> 19:44.038
If you want to ask her out, you should give it a try, though.

341
19:44.705 --> 19:46.624
-Nah. -Why not?

342
19:46.707 --> 19:47.833
I've got to study.

343
19:48.709 --> 19:51.212
Besides, I've never really been into girls.

344
19:51.879 --> 19:52.880
What?

345
19:54.715 --> 19:57.218
It doesn't mean I'm into guys, though.

346
20:00.346 --> 20:01.347
I'm just busy.

347
20:02.139 --> 20:03.140
Okay.

348
20:03.641 --> 20:04.975
I need to study. Study.

349
20:05.059 --> 20:06.769
Sure. Suit yourself.

350
20:08.395 --> 20:12.942
The fan and actuator designs seem fine, but we can't get the heat under control.

351
20:13.025 --> 20:15.402
Maybe the torque demand in the motor is too high?

352
20:15.486 --> 20:16.529
[Taeho] Mmm.

353
20:16.612 --> 20:18.864
The battery is running a little hot too.

354
20:18.948 --> 20:20.825
Well, we'll have to rerun the simulation.

355
20:21.951 --> 20:25.871
We have to get the motor temperature below 80 degrees, no matter what. Okay?

356
20:25.955 --> 20:28.624
So should we redesign the cooling system?

357
20:28.707 --> 20:30.751
If tweaking it doesn't work, we'll have to.

358
20:33.629 --> 20:35.422
And...

359
20:35.923 --> 20:38.259
the control algorithm optimization.

360
20:38.759 --> 20:40.553
Youjin, do you want to read up on it and try?

361
20:41.136 --> 20:43.222
-Hmm? Me? -Yeah.

362
20:43.305 --> 20:46.141
But Lim Youjin doesn't know anything, so how is she supposed to--

363
20:48.394 --> 20:49.395
Well...

364
20:50.187 --> 20:53.148
I've got the data downloaded, Ms. Lim.

365
20:54.441 --> 20:56.235
You can look it over and give it a try.

366
20:56.318 --> 20:59.822
Okay, good. If you run into any issues, just ask Taeho or me.

367
20:59.905 --> 21:02.408
And take a look at Sejin's data too.

368
21:02.491 --> 21:04.243
-Okay. -Good.

369
21:04.952 --> 21:06.328
-Let's wrap it up here. -[Hangyeol] Okay.

370
21:06.412 --> 21:07.663
-Sure. -[Taeho] All right.

371
21:10.916 --> 21:12.001
[Taeho] Gyeol. Chan.

372
21:12.084 --> 21:13.085
[Hangyeol and Chansoo] Yes?

373
21:13.168 --> 21:16.213
Let's go to the control room for a quick check on the load torque.

374
21:16.297 --> 21:17.715
-[Hangyeol] Okay. -[Taeho] Okay.

375
21:20.092 --> 21:22.219
-[Hangyeol] We'll be right back. -[Minjae] Okay.

376
21:23.554 --> 21:24.638
[clears throat]

377
21:25.389 --> 21:26.849
[door opens]

378
21:28.809 --> 21:29.810
Lim Youjin.

379
21:30.936 --> 21:32.062
What's up?

380
21:34.023 --> 21:36.734
I sent you an email, so give it a read.

381
21:36.817 --> 21:38.777
It's the paper I downloaded from the archive

382
21:38.861 --> 21:42.531
and the comments I added after reading it. Take a look.

383
21:43.407 --> 21:44.617
Okay.

384
21:45.326 --> 21:46.327
Well, thanks.

385
21:54.043 --> 21:57.254
Do you happen to have some time this week?

386
21:58.714 --> 21:59.798
Why?

387
21:59.882 --> 22:03.218
I was just wondering if you wanted to grab a bite sometime.

388
22:04.386 --> 22:06.138
You and me? Why?

389
22:06.221 --> 22:07.348
What do you mean, why?

390
22:08.140 --> 22:09.600
We're in the same cohort,

391
22:10.893 --> 22:12.728
but we've been kind of distant.

392
22:12.811 --> 22:15.397
I thought we could change that and get along. That's all.

393
22:20.694 --> 22:21.820
Oh.

394
22:21.904 --> 22:24.239
Yeah. Well, whatever. Okay.

395
22:29.203 --> 22:32.456
If just the two of us is awkward, you can bring your friend too.

396
22:35.626 --> 22:36.627
[Sejin sighs]

397
22:36.710 --> 22:37.711
[scoffs]

398
22:40.381 --> 22:41.715
Ah...

399
22:42.633 --> 22:44.802
Subin is my best friend.

400
22:45.803 --> 22:49.765
But how could I set her up with that nutjob Kim Sejin?

401
22:49.848 --> 22:50.849
You think I'm crazy?

402
22:50.933 --> 22:53.102
You're not setting her up with him.

403
22:53.185 --> 22:55.938
It's just a casual meal. That's all.

404
22:56.021 --> 22:57.898
It's the same thing.

405
22:58.565 --> 23:00.526
You're basically asking my friend to... What's it called?

406
23:01.110 --> 23:03.404
Right, jump on a grenade.

407
23:03.487 --> 23:05.406
You don't care if the grenade kills my friend.

408
23:05.489 --> 23:07.408
Don't put it like that.

409
23:08.325 --> 23:09.326
Tell me.

410
23:10.244 --> 23:12.663
If Subin and I were drowning, who would you save?

411
23:14.498 --> 23:16.083
I'd save my friend.

412
23:16.166 --> 23:17.376
I'd save Subin.

413
23:22.297 --> 23:23.298
You...

414
23:24.925 --> 23:26.677
I wasn't going to tell you this.

415
23:27.469 --> 23:29.722
I wasn't going to tell you this

416
23:29.805 --> 23:32.433
because I knew you'd go berserk and want to kill Kim Sejin.

417
23:33.934 --> 23:35.769
Do you know what happened this morning?

418
23:36.478 --> 23:38.605
Why? What happened?

419
23:39.356 --> 23:42.234
Well, when I woke up in the morning, Kim Sejin...

420
23:44.194 --> 23:45.946
was sleeping in my bed.

421
23:46.030 --> 23:47.740
[♪ comical music playing]

422
23:50.200 --> 23:53.203
I mean, he said he was going to sleep in the living room.

423
23:53.287 --> 23:56.040
But when I woke up this morning, the punk was lying next to me.

424
23:58.876 --> 24:00.836
What the... Even I haven't slept in that bed yet.

425
24:00.919 --> 24:02.796
You have no idea how shocked I was.

426
24:03.380 --> 24:05.507
Did you get hurt anywhere? Are you feeling okay?

427
24:05.591 --> 24:08.260
No, I didn't get hurt.

428
24:08.343 --> 24:09.344
But...

429
24:10.095 --> 24:11.472
it didn't feel good.

430
24:12.181 --> 24:14.641
Did Kim Sejin touch you?

431
24:14.725 --> 24:17.394
I have no idea. I was asleep.

432
24:17.478 --> 24:20.522
[sighs in exasperation] But you're mine!

433
24:20.606 --> 24:23.817
And you'd still save Subin over me?

434
24:26.236 --> 24:29.698
He just wants to grab a bite with her. It's not a date or anything.

435
24:30.324 --> 24:35.079
After that, those two can take it from there. Okay?

436
24:35.746 --> 24:36.747
[sighs]

437
24:43.670 --> 24:45.756
Come on, you've seen him too.

438
24:46.340 --> 24:48.133
He's not bad-looking.

439
24:48.217 --> 24:49.927
He didn't seem like a total weirdo, right?

440
24:50.594 --> 24:53.722
It's just that I'm not really in a place for that right now.

441
24:53.806 --> 24:55.599
And I'm not really looking to date.

442
24:55.682 --> 24:58.685
Subin, do me a favor just this once. Please?

443
25:01.480 --> 25:05.442
If you really don't like him, just stay for 10 minutes,

444
25:05.526 --> 25:08.362
then say you have a headache and go home.

445
25:09.154 --> 25:10.572
Wouldn't that be too rude?

446
25:10.656 --> 25:12.366
It's okay. It's not rude.

447
25:13.117 --> 25:16.411
Just stay for 10 minutes and leave. Okay?

448
25:16.495 --> 25:17.663
Hmm?

449
25:22.209 --> 25:23.210
Oh?

450
25:23.710 --> 25:24.711
-Here. -Hey.

451
25:28.715 --> 25:30.134
-Here. -[Minjae] Okay.

452
25:35.097 --> 25:36.098
Hello.

453
25:38.308 --> 25:39.434
-There. -Please sit.

454
25:43.981 --> 25:46.900
So this is Jung Subin.

455
25:46.984 --> 25:49.611
And this is my lab mate, Kim Sejin, who's in my cohort.

456
25:50.779 --> 25:51.780
Hello.

457
25:54.199 --> 25:58.203
Well, we met at the wedding, right? We said "hi" then.

458
25:58.287 --> 26:00.789
Ah. Yeah, I remember.

459
26:00.873 --> 26:02.791
We said "hi" on the bus too. Both of us.

460
26:03.417 --> 26:04.418
Yes.

461
26:05.043 --> 26:07.045
[Youjin] Oh, so you've met a few times already.

462
26:07.129 --> 26:09.339
No need to feel awkward, then.

463
26:11.884 --> 26:13.385
-Here you go. -Thank you.

464
26:13.468 --> 26:15.762
I hear everything is good, so pick whatever you want.

465
26:17.264 --> 26:19.933
Yeah, it's Sejin's treat, so go for the most expensive one.

466
26:20.017 --> 26:21.602
Yeah. Anything you like.

467
26:23.187 --> 26:24.938
[Subin] Hmm.

468
26:27.983 --> 26:30.027
-[mouthing] Not yet. -[mouthing] Why?

469
26:33.864 --> 26:35.824
-By the way... -Yes?

470
26:35.908 --> 26:38.535
Youjin and I have something to do.

471
26:39.411 --> 26:40.704
So I think we should get going.

472
26:42.539 --> 26:44.875
Why? Is it urgent?

473
26:44.958 --> 26:48.337
The professor asked us to do something, so we should go to the campus.

474
26:49.713 --> 26:51.715
Well, I guess it can't be helped, then.

475
26:52.507 --> 26:56.094
Yeah, I guess you'll have to eat without us today.

476
26:56.178 --> 26:58.931
Well, we can always get together another time.

477
26:59.014 --> 27:00.974
We all know each other, anyway.

478
27:01.058 --> 27:02.267
Yeah.

479
27:02.351 --> 27:04.394
We can always get together again sometime.

480
27:04.478 --> 27:07.481
All right. Now, shall we?

481
27:08.065 --> 27:09.066
Sorry, guys.

482
27:09.149 --> 27:10.150
[grunts]

483
27:11.944 --> 27:13.278
Come on. Let's go, Youjin.

484
27:14.947 --> 27:15.948
Let's go.

485
27:18.200 --> 27:20.202
-Okay, Minjae. -No, don't get up.

486
27:21.620 --> 27:23.121
All right. Enjoy your meal.

487
27:23.205 --> 27:24.456
-Take care. -Thanks.

488
27:32.965 --> 27:33.966
[softly] Let's go.

489
27:36.009 --> 27:37.135
What? Don't.

490
27:37.844 --> 27:40.263
Pick one. Do you want to save Subin or me?

491
27:41.473 --> 27:44.309
-I'll save Subin. I'll save her. -Don't be like that. Come here.

492
27:44.393 --> 27:45.602
[groans softly]

493
28:12.295 --> 28:13.755
What would you like to have?

494
28:14.881 --> 28:15.882
Uh...

495
28:22.597 --> 28:24.349
I'm sorry...

496
28:25.600 --> 28:27.561
but I have a headache.

497
28:28.770 --> 28:30.647
I think I need to go back home.

498
28:33.400 --> 28:34.401
Oh...

499
28:37.738 --> 28:39.239
Is it really bad?

500
28:43.577 --> 28:46.538
Do you have a fever or anything like that?

501
28:46.621 --> 28:48.832
I don't have a fever.

502
28:49.624 --> 28:50.625
It's just a headache.

503
28:50.709 --> 28:52.836
[♪ theme song playing]

504
28:52.919 --> 28:55.839
Just sit here for a minute. I saw a pharmacy on the way here.

505
28:55.922 --> 28:57.132
-I'll be right back. -It's okay.

506
28:57.215 --> 28:58.341
I'll go get you some medicine.

507
28:59.051 --> 29:00.927
Please take it before you go.

508
29:01.011 --> 29:02.512
-No, I'm okay. -I'll be real quick.

509
29:58.151 --> 29:59.152
Thank you.

510
30:00.821 --> 30:02.405
Goodbye. Hello.

511
30:02.489 --> 30:04.282
-Headache meds, please. -For a headache?

512
30:05.450 --> 30:06.451
Uh...

513
30:07.202 --> 30:09.412
-Something that works fast... -Yes.

514
30:10.205 --> 30:11.540
...and is gentle on the stomach.

515
30:11.623 --> 30:13.625
Sure. Got it.

516
30:14.251 --> 30:16.211
Something mild.

517
30:16.294 --> 30:17.504
Right, this one is mild.

518
30:31.726 --> 30:33.228
[panting] Here's some medicine for your headache.

519
30:34.354 --> 30:35.480
You're all sweaty.

520
30:35.564 --> 30:38.316
How far did you go to get this?

521
30:39.568 --> 30:41.403
Not too far. It was right around the corner.

522
30:41.987 --> 30:43.196
It only took a minute.

523
30:48.743 --> 30:49.744
Take it.

524
30:50.370 --> 30:52.164
Then you can head home.

525
30:56.084 --> 30:57.085
One tablet.

526
30:57.627 --> 30:58.628
One tablet?

527
31:10.724 --> 31:11.975
Would you like to order?

528
31:16.354 --> 31:18.190
We'll come back another time.

529
31:18.690 --> 31:19.858
I'm sorry.

530
31:19.941 --> 31:20.942
Oh...

531
31:28.491 --> 31:29.492
Let's go.

532
31:31.203 --> 31:32.204
Okay.

533
31:42.339 --> 31:43.340
Say "ah."

534
31:48.011 --> 31:49.012
What should we do now?

535
31:53.183 --> 31:54.392
How about a movie?

536
31:54.476 --> 31:55.602
-A movie? -Yeah.

537
31:59.814 --> 32:00.982
It's too...

538
32:02.234 --> 32:03.235
crowded.

539
32:04.945 --> 32:07.614
Should we just watch a movie at home?

540
32:09.199 --> 32:11.326
Okay. But which movie?

541
32:11.910 --> 32:13.245
Is there anything you want to watch?

542
32:13.870 --> 32:14.871
Anything's fine.

543
32:17.415 --> 32:19.584
-Something sexy? -Jeez...

544
32:20.627 --> 32:21.711
Why?

545
32:21.795 --> 32:23.421
Are you scared I might eat you alive?

546
32:24.297 --> 32:26.216
What do you mean, scared?

547
32:26.716 --> 32:28.009
Of course not.

548
32:28.885 --> 32:30.387
-[clears throat] -You're cute.

549
32:33.431 --> 32:34.432
Hey.

550
32:35.016 --> 32:36.434
People are watching.

551
32:36.977 --> 32:38.228
-Don't do that. -Why?

552
32:38.728 --> 32:41.564
Fine. Let's save that kiss for when we get home, Minjae.

553
32:45.360 --> 32:48.989
I specifically asked for a mild one.

554
32:52.200 --> 32:55.495
You should go home and get some sleep.

555
32:56.538 --> 33:00.041
When you wake up, you'll feel a lot better.

556
33:01.793 --> 33:02.794
Okay.

557
33:05.505 --> 33:08.925
Give it some time, and if you still don't feel better,

558
33:09.009 --> 33:11.553
you should see a doctor.

559
33:14.848 --> 33:15.849
I'm sorry.

560
33:16.850 --> 33:17.851
What?

561
33:19.436 --> 33:20.437
Ah.

562
33:21.354 --> 33:22.564
Don't be.

563
33:22.647 --> 33:24.607
You're just sick. There's no need to apologize.

564
33:26.568 --> 33:29.988
We can always grab a bite another time.

565
33:32.490 --> 33:33.491
It's okay.

566
33:35.994 --> 33:37.412
The taxi is here.

567
33:47.172 --> 33:48.173
Get in.

568
33:49.632 --> 33:52.385
-I'm sorry. -You don't have to be. It's really okay.

569
33:53.678 --> 33:54.888
Well, let's make sure...

570
33:56.473 --> 33:57.474
we get a meal

571
33:58.266 --> 33:59.559
together next time.

572
33:59.642 --> 34:01.394
I'll treat you to something good.

573
34:01.478 --> 34:04.272
No. I'll treat you to something even better.

574
34:04.356 --> 34:06.358
[♪ pleasant music playing]

575
34:07.567 --> 34:10.403
Sure, well... We can do that too.

576
34:10.487 --> 34:11.488
Mmm.

577
34:17.911 --> 34:18.953
Excuse me, sir.

578
34:19.037 --> 34:21.289
My friend is not feeling well,

579
34:21.373 --> 34:24.042
so please drive carefully.

580
34:24.125 --> 34:26.002
[driver] All right. I'll get her home safely.

581
34:27.420 --> 34:28.838
Have a safe trip home.

582
35:17.429 --> 35:18.638
[sighs]

583
35:34.696 --> 35:35.697
So?

584
35:35.780 --> 35:36.865
How did it go?

585
35:38.575 --> 35:40.702
She had a headache, so she just left--

586
35:40.785 --> 35:42.912
[mouthing] It's Sejin. Kim Sejin.

587
35:44.456 --> 35:45.457
Yeah.

588
35:46.040 --> 35:47.834
Yeah, she left.

589
35:52.672 --> 35:54.799
We can always grab a bite another time.

590
35:56.843 --> 35:57.844
It's fine.

591
35:58.344 --> 36:00.013
Yeah, things happen.

592
36:01.347 --> 36:02.974
But why did she suddenly get a headache?

593
36:05.143 --> 36:06.227
Okay.

594
36:06.311 --> 36:08.813
So she went home, and what about you?

595
36:09.564 --> 36:11.691
So I'm just by myself now.

596
36:12.233 --> 36:13.359
Where are you, Minjae?

597
36:13.443 --> 36:15.320
-Are you still nearby? -Me?

598
36:15.862 --> 36:17.655
I'm not here.

599
36:17.739 --> 36:20.366
No, I mean, when I said, "I'm not here,"

600
36:21.034 --> 36:23.203
I'm already on my way home.

601
36:25.705 --> 36:26.956
Youjin?

602
36:27.749 --> 36:30.251
Youjin left too.

603
36:31.002 --> 36:33.963
-[mouthing] School. Say I went to school. -School. She went to school.

604
36:34.047 --> 36:36.382
I think so. She said she was going to school.

605
36:38.218 --> 36:39.594
[mouthing] Just hang up.

606
36:39.677 --> 36:40.845
Hang up.

607
36:40.929 --> 36:43.431
Hey, Sejin, I'm getting another call. I've got to go.

608
36:43.515 --> 36:44.516
Okay.

609
36:45.016 --> 36:46.017
Well, then...

610
36:47.018 --> 36:49.312
I'll tell you more about it when we meet.

611
36:51.314 --> 36:52.315
Bye.

612
37:01.407 --> 37:03.243
So did you decide what movie you want to watch?

613
37:03.910 --> 37:05.620
I told you, something sexy.

614
37:05.703 --> 37:08.540
-Come on. -Oh, come on.

615
37:08.623 --> 37:11.209
-[phone vibrating] -Why are you suddenly so into sexy movies?

616
37:12.502 --> 37:13.503
Oh...

617
37:13.586 --> 37:14.629
Who is it?

618
37:14.712 --> 37:15.713
It's Kim Sejin.

619
37:15.797 --> 37:17.090
I don't need to answer it.

620
37:18.049 --> 37:19.133
What should we watch?

621
37:19.717 --> 37:21.719
I don't know. I know nothing.

622
37:21.803 --> 37:23.346
[Youjin] You must like at least one movie.

623
37:23.429 --> 37:25.348
[Minjae] One movie... Then what about you?

624
37:44.200 --> 37:46.202
[♪ bright music plays on TV]

625
37:52.876 --> 37:54.335
-[doorbell chiming] -Huh?

626
37:55.712 --> 37:58.089
-That must be our tteokbokki. -No, don't get up.

627
37:58.923 --> 38:00.049
I'll go get it.

628
38:03.469 --> 38:04.846
[softly] Jeez.

629
38:05.722 --> 38:07.682
What? What are you doing here?

630
38:07.765 --> 38:09.100
Hi, Minjae.

631
38:09.684 --> 38:10.810
You're home.

632
38:10.894 --> 38:12.395
Of course, I am. It's my home.

633
38:13.146 --> 38:14.564
Where else would I be?

634
38:15.773 --> 38:16.900
Well, it's just...

635
38:18.526 --> 38:21.279
I thought I'd give you a detailed update on the blind date.

636
38:23.239 --> 38:24.490
And I need to tell you something.

637
38:24.574 --> 38:25.575
Okay.

638
38:26.743 --> 38:29.495
-I'll tell you inside. -What? Inside where? No, say it here.

639
38:29.621 --> 38:31.664
Just say it here. Go ahead. What is it?

640
38:32.206 --> 38:33.207
It's a long story.

641
38:33.291 --> 38:34.459
Make it short, then.

642
38:35.460 --> 38:38.630
-Let's get inside and-- -Come on. Don't be like this. I'm busy.

643
38:38.713 --> 38:40.173
-[elevator dings] -I have tons of work to do.

644
38:40.256 --> 38:41.507
Just hurry up and say it.

645
38:44.093 --> 38:45.803
Here's your volcano tteokbokki.

646
38:45.887 --> 38:47.597
[sighs] Oh.

647
38:51.309 --> 38:52.560
You ordered tteokbokki?

648
38:52.644 --> 38:53.853
For yourself?

649
38:53.937 --> 38:56.981
Yeah, I love tteokbokki. I ordered it for myself. Why?

650
38:57.523 --> 38:58.608
What? What is it?

651
38:58.691 --> 39:00.068
Here, the tteokbokki...

652
39:00.151 --> 39:02.195
-That... -You can give it to me. Thank you.

653
39:02.278 --> 39:04.364
For God's sake.

654
39:05.740 --> 39:06.741
Go.

655
39:10.453 --> 39:12.956
Yeah, give it to me. Okay. Thank you. Give it to me.

656
39:13.039 --> 39:15.083
Give it to me and go. What are you doing?

657
39:15.166 --> 39:16.459
Can I have some tteokbokki?

658
39:16.542 --> 39:19.545
-Just go. Come on, give me that. -I'm hungry too. Let's eat together.

659
39:20.213 --> 39:22.423
Order some with your own money! Now give me that.

660
39:22.507 --> 39:24.884
Come on, let's eat together. Food's better together.

661
39:24.968 --> 39:27.428
What do you mean, eat together? No, get out. God!

662
39:27.512 --> 39:30.473
Seriously. For God's sake, jeez.

663
39:31.391 --> 39:33.851
Fine. Eat it and get out, okay?

664
39:36.312 --> 39:39.023
You just show up out of nowhere and ask for my tteokbokki?

665
39:39.649 --> 39:40.650
Come on, give me that.

666
39:42.860 --> 39:45.363
Why haven't you eaten-- Hey, why are you going there?

667
39:45.446 --> 39:46.823
What? Why?

668
39:46.906 --> 39:48.074
What are you doing?

669
39:49.325 --> 39:50.576
What are you looking for?

670
39:50.660 --> 39:51.744
Huh?

671
39:52.829 --> 39:53.871
What are you doing?

672
39:55.915 --> 39:57.125
What's this about?

673
39:57.750 --> 39:58.960
-Well... -Yeah.

674
40:00.586 --> 40:02.588
I thought I heard something.

675
40:03.631 --> 40:05.091
What are you talking about?

676
40:09.053 --> 40:10.930
-Now, get out. -Was I just imagining it?

677
40:11.014 --> 40:13.766
Yes, you were. You were imagining it. Now, get out. Go.

678
40:14.684 --> 40:17.895
Come here. You said you were hungry. Let's eat.

679
40:17.979 --> 40:19.522
Where are you going now? Jeez.

680
40:20.023 --> 40:22.608
Why on earth are you doing this? What is it?

681
40:23.192 --> 40:25.486
Tell me. I'll find it for you. What is it?

682
40:25.570 --> 40:26.696
-It's just... -What?

683
40:27.321 --> 40:29.240
I think I hear something.

684
40:29.866 --> 40:31.367
It sounds like a person.

685
40:31.451 --> 40:34.162
What? There's no one here. You're just hearing things.

686
40:34.245 --> 40:35.246
Exactly.

687
40:35.997 --> 40:37.165
[sighs in exasperation]

688
40:37.707 --> 40:38.708
It can't be...

689
40:40.418 --> 40:42.170
these guys talking, can it?

690
40:42.712 --> 40:45.089
-What are you talking... -That'd be too creepy.

691
40:46.841 --> 40:48.301
Stop the nonsense and come here.

692
40:48.384 --> 40:50.553
-Wait. -Why?

693
40:50.636 --> 40:52.513
See? I can hear it right now.

694
40:52.597 --> 40:53.931
I can hear a person talking...

695
40:55.349 --> 40:58.019
-and some music. -All right, I hear it. Come here.

696
41:03.024 --> 41:05.777
You said you were hungry. Hurry up and eat, then leave.

697
41:05.860 --> 41:06.861
I have a lot of things to do.

698
41:07.904 --> 41:09.322
Come on, eat up. Go on.

699
41:12.784 --> 41:13.785
What?

700
41:14.410 --> 41:15.453
Are you leaving?

701
41:18.122 --> 41:19.123
I need to use the bathroom.

702
41:19.207 --> 41:20.208
Go ahead.

703
41:24.962 --> 41:26.130
Hey, Sejin.

704
41:27.256 --> 41:28.674
Is this what you were hearing?

705
41:28.758 --> 41:30.009
-Huh? -[increases volume]

706
41:30.760 --> 41:32.095
This? From my laptop?

707
41:32.804 --> 41:34.472
Ah...

708
41:35.848 --> 41:37.475
It was the movie.

709
41:37.558 --> 41:39.685
[Minjae] Yeah, this was the person you were hearing.

710
42:01.124 --> 42:02.125
[whispering] Youjin.

711
42:02.208 --> 42:04.544
Youjin, are you okay?

712
42:04.627 --> 42:07.088
-[whispering] Can I go out? -Come out now. Now.

713
42:10.967 --> 42:11.968
Right, Youjin.

714
42:13.177 --> 42:14.679
Your shoes are in the washing machine.

715
42:18.266 --> 42:19.308
Bye.

716
42:19.392 --> 42:20.393
Okay, bye.

717
42:20.476 --> 42:21.477
Call me.

718
42:21.561 --> 42:23.604
Hey, the door. Be careful.

719
42:24.147 --> 42:25.565
[door lock chimes]

720
42:25.648 --> 42:26.649
[Minjae coughs]

721
42:27.650 --> 42:30.403
-[dishes clattering] -[continues coughing]

722
42:32.029 --> 42:34.323
-Gosh, this keeps falling. [coughs] -[door lock chimes]

723
42:39.704 --> 42:40.705
[sighs]

724
43:01.017 --> 43:02.018
[inhaling sharply]

725
43:04.645 --> 43:07.148
It's pretty spicy, isn't it? The volcano one.

726
43:08.191 --> 43:10.526
The rice balls should help with the heat. Have some.

727
43:12.653 --> 43:13.779
Aren't you going to eat?

728
43:13.863 --> 43:15.198
Me?

729
43:15.281 --> 43:17.200
I'll eat too, later.

730
43:21.329 --> 43:23.748
Right. So how did the blind date go?

731
43:25.666 --> 43:26.667
Hmm.

732
43:28.878 --> 43:30.046
Subin...

733
43:30.129 --> 43:31.130
Yeah.

734
43:31.214 --> 43:34.175
She suddenly said her head hurt.

735
43:35.051 --> 43:37.720
-A headache. -Yeah, why did her head hurt?

736
43:39.430 --> 43:44.018
Sensitive, delicate women tend to get headaches a lot.

737
43:44.101 --> 43:45.311
Low blood pressure, too.

738
43:46.354 --> 43:48.940
Man, you really do know everything, don't you?

739
43:49.023 --> 43:50.733
I do know a lot of things.

740
43:50.816 --> 43:52.818
[both giggling]

741
43:55.363 --> 43:56.614
Well, anyway...

742
43:57.865 --> 43:59.200
She had a headache,

743
43:59.784 --> 44:01.160
so I got her some medicine.

744
44:01.869 --> 44:05.164
We said we'd grab a bite another time.

745
44:05.248 --> 44:06.415
Okay, good.

746
44:10.544 --> 44:12.129
But then...

747
44:12.964 --> 44:14.131
Yeah?

748
44:17.176 --> 44:18.886
After I saw Subin off...

749
44:22.056 --> 44:23.599
I saw something.

750
44:24.600 --> 44:26.310
What did you see? What was it?

751
44:33.526 --> 44:34.527
[inhales]

752
44:36.153 --> 44:37.530
Nothing. [sighs]

753
44:42.618 --> 44:44.954
Hey, don't be so disappointed, okay?

754
44:45.037 --> 44:46.664
At least you've met her now.

755
44:47.248 --> 44:48.958
You can always see her again, right?

756
44:49.041 --> 44:51.127
You'll get another chance, Sejin.

757
44:56.132 --> 44:57.425
You're a pretty great guy.

758
44:57.508 --> 45:00.469
You're good-looking, kind, smart,

759
45:01.429 --> 45:02.430
hardworking,

760
45:03.556 --> 45:05.057
and you've got a great academic background.

761
45:06.892 --> 45:09.729
So don't rush things. Just take your time.

762
45:09.812 --> 45:13.607
If you're sincere with her and keep treating her with kindness,

763
45:13.691 --> 45:16.444
she'll eventually see what a great guy you are.

764
45:22.616 --> 45:23.868
-By the way... -Yeah.

765
45:26.454 --> 45:30.958
Even if I treat her sincerely with kindness,

766
45:31.667 --> 45:38.090
she can still deceive me, betray me, and lie to me, right?

767
45:38.174 --> 45:39.175
What?

768
45:40.426 --> 45:41.427
I mean...

769
45:43.346 --> 45:46.557
People say you should never trust anyone, you know.

770
45:47.850 --> 45:50.561
I don't know what that's got to do with this, though.

771
45:51.896 --> 45:54.482
Well, by that logic, the Bible also says,

772
45:56.275 --> 45:59.278
"If someone strikes you on one cheek, offer them the other."

773
45:59.362 --> 46:01.864
And the Buddha said, "Always show compassion to others."

774
46:01.947 --> 46:04.533
There are good sayings like those, too.

775
46:06.369 --> 46:07.370
Yeah.

776
46:08.496 --> 46:09.914
There are, but still...

777
46:11.123 --> 46:12.458
[scoffing]

778
46:12.541 --> 46:15.836
So don't rush it.

779
46:15.920 --> 46:19.590
Just take things a little slower, and don't put any pressure on her.

780
46:19.673 --> 46:22.593
If you do that, I think it'll work out.

781
46:27.223 --> 46:28.224
Gosh, it's spicy.

782
46:32.603 --> 46:34.647
-You should have some. [clears throat] -Yeah, okay.

783
46:42.446 --> 46:44.448
[♪ intriguing music playing]

784
47:04.260 --> 47:05.719
[sighs]

785
47:09.390 --> 47:10.599
He went to bed early.

786
47:13.561 --> 47:14.562
Maybe he's tired.

787
47:36.959 --> 47:38.335
[shuffling]

788
47:40.254 --> 47:42.173
[rustling]

789
48:06.363 --> 48:09.825
ENGINEERING BUILDING 3

790
48:09.909 --> 48:10.993
[Chansoo] Minjae.

791
48:12.203 --> 48:15.789
I have plans today. Can I leave early?

792
48:15.873 --> 48:17.666
[Taeho] It's past 5:00, anyway.

793
48:17.750 --> 48:20.377
That's not even leaving early. Just go.

794
48:22.379 --> 48:23.422
[quietly] No?

795
48:24.256 --> 48:27.593
Well, if you're done, you can go.

796
48:29.887 --> 48:32.765
All right, thanks for your hard work on the experiment today.

797
48:33.432 --> 48:35.059
-Let's get off early. -[Taeho] Okay.

798
48:35.142 --> 48:37.520
-[Chansoo] Okay. -Thank you.

799
48:39.980 --> 48:41.190
Let's go.

800
48:42.900 --> 48:43.901
[Youjin] Bye.

801
48:49.198 --> 48:50.199
Bye.

802
48:50.991 --> 48:51.992
Bye.

803
48:54.411 --> 48:55.663
Youjin, aren't you going home?

804
48:56.830 --> 48:59.708
I need to organize the data I got before I leave.

805
48:59.792 --> 49:01.418
I see. And you, Sejin?

806
49:01.502 --> 49:03.212
Yeah, I also have some work to finish.

807
49:03.295 --> 49:05.756
Yeah? Don't stay too late. I'll get going.

808
49:06.340 --> 49:07.967
-Bye. -Bye.

809
49:17.726 --> 49:18.727
Lim Youjin.

810
49:19.353 --> 49:20.354
What?

811
49:20.980 --> 49:23.232
Do you have a lot of work? When will you be done?

812
49:23.315 --> 49:24.942
Why do you ask when I'll be done?

813
49:25.526 --> 49:27.278
We said we'd grab a bite together, remember?

814
49:29.238 --> 49:30.614
I have something to tell you too.

815
49:31.740 --> 49:33.158
What is it?

816
49:36.662 --> 49:38.664
[♪ pleasant song playing over speakers]

817
50:04.481 --> 50:05.816
What is it that you wanted to tell me?

818
50:09.570 --> 50:10.821
You said you'd tell me after the meal.

819
50:11.864 --> 50:13.157
We're done now, so shoot.

820
50:16.452 --> 50:17.578
I saw everything.

821
50:18.329 --> 50:20.289
You and Minjae are walking hand in hand.

822
50:25.836 --> 50:26.837
Are you two dating?

823
50:28.505 --> 50:30.382
No, we're not.

824
50:31.175 --> 50:32.843
Then why were you holding hands?

825
50:35.262 --> 50:36.347
Could it be...

826
50:37.640 --> 50:39.308
that you were mistaken?

827
50:41.435 --> 50:43.520
And even if I'm dating him,

828
50:44.021 --> 50:45.648
it's not something I have to tell you.

829
50:47.775 --> 50:50.194
Or why don't you ask Minjae yourself?

830
50:50.277 --> 50:53.447
Actually, I was going to ask Minjae about it.

831
50:56.116 --> 50:58.077
And do you know what he said?

832
51:01.538 --> 51:02.665
What did he say?

833
51:04.166 --> 51:05.167
That if...

834
51:06.794 --> 51:10.005
you're sincere with someone and treat them with kindness,

835
51:10.089 --> 51:12.675
they'll eventually see it.

836
51:15.219 --> 51:16.220
What?

837
51:17.513 --> 51:22.142
That's how naive and innocent he is.

838
51:24.144 --> 51:26.814
He has no idea that the world doesn't work that way.

839
51:27.815 --> 51:30.526
He's kind and principled, but he's completely clueless.

840
51:30.609 --> 51:34.029
He's nothing like you.

841
51:42.246 --> 51:46.750
I don't know why you're trying to get close with Minjae.

842
51:49.753 --> 51:52.297
Actually, I do.

843
51:53.382 --> 51:56.301
But seriously, stop that. You really can't do that.

844
51:59.096 --> 52:02.182
-What do you mean? I can't do what? -Well, obviously...

845
52:05.686 --> 52:07.646
Stay away from Minjae from now on.

846
52:11.734 --> 52:14.111
Let's be honest. You're just using him.

847
52:14.194 --> 52:16.196
What does he have that I could possibly use?

848
52:16.280 --> 52:18.240
Power. His power.

849
52:18.323 --> 52:22.327
What freaking power does he have? He can't even get me out of work early.

850
52:22.411 --> 52:24.329
He's our lab lead, after all.

851
52:24.413 --> 52:27.958
He could give you the best projects and special guidance on your papers.

852
52:28.041 --> 52:29.084
Something like that.

853
52:29.168 --> 52:31.170
Wow, I'm just speechless.

854
52:32.629 --> 52:34.840
Now that I know what's going on, you've got to end it.

855
52:36.592 --> 52:37.760
Let Minjae go.

856
52:39.052 --> 52:42.931
He's not someone you can look down on and use for your own benefit like that.

857
52:45.684 --> 52:47.060
I know I'm overstepping,

858
52:47.644 --> 52:50.731
and I'm not usually one to stick my nose in other people's business.

859
52:51.440 --> 52:54.485
But this time, I have to step in. That's why I'm telling you this.

860
52:54.568 --> 52:55.736
[sighing]

861
52:55.819 --> 52:57.237
Gosh, my head hurts.

862
52:57.321 --> 52:58.572
Ah...

863
52:58.655 --> 53:00.157
I'll be honest with you.

864
53:00.783 --> 53:02.409
I don't have many friends,

865
53:03.160 --> 53:05.913
and there aren't many people I genuinely like.

866
53:07.414 --> 53:09.750
But Minjae...

867
53:12.377 --> 53:13.378
I like him quite a lot.

868
53:13.462 --> 53:14.588
What?

869
53:14.671 --> 53:16.799
I mean, I like him as a person.

870
53:16.882 --> 53:18.091
I admire him.

871
53:20.177 --> 53:23.096
I can't just watch while someone as shameless, sly,

872
53:23.180 --> 53:26.683
and mean as you walks all over him. So end it now.

873
53:31.480 --> 53:33.232
I don't care whether you watch or not.

874
53:33.816 --> 53:34.817
I've got to go.

875
53:34.900 --> 53:36.527
So I've got a proposal for you.

876
53:37.361 --> 53:38.362
Let's call it...

877
53:39.238 --> 53:41.698
a challenge to a duel.

878
53:41.782 --> 53:43.617
Duels are supposed to be fought with guns.

879
53:45.118 --> 53:48.413
Lucky for you, guns are illegal in this country, Kim Sejin.

880
53:48.997 --> 53:51.124
Whoever wins gets to do whatever they want.

881
53:52.167 --> 53:55.754
If I win, you stay away from Minjae.

882
53:56.922 --> 53:57.923
And if you win...

883
54:01.426 --> 54:02.928
I'll quit the lab,

884
54:04.513 --> 54:05.722
and go back to Daejeon.

885
54:09.184 --> 54:11.270
You choose what we compete in.

886
54:11.353 --> 54:13.230
What... FIFA?

887
54:15.107 --> 54:16.108
StarCraft?

888
54:16.692 --> 54:17.693
League of Legends?

889
54:18.318 --> 54:19.695
Anything you're good at.

890
54:20.946 --> 54:22.489
It doesn't have to be a video game.

891
54:22.573 --> 54:26.076
We could solve math problems, memorize words, or things like that.

892
54:26.994 --> 54:30.497
I'm even fine with a drinking game.

893
54:31.957 --> 54:35.878
Pick anything you're confident in, anything you think you can beat me at.

894
54:37.796 --> 54:41.174
But we're not telling Minjae or anyone else.

895
54:41.967 --> 54:42.968
What do you say?

896
54:45.554 --> 54:47.514
They'd think I'm crazy if I told them.

897
54:48.807 --> 54:49.808
Hey.

898
54:50.892 --> 54:53.979
I should've recorded all that and played it for Minjae.

899
54:54.688 --> 54:55.689
Too bad.

900
54:56.773 --> 54:57.774
Are you not in?

901
54:58.650 --> 54:59.651
I'm heading out.

902
55:04.781 --> 55:05.782
[groans]

903
55:15.959 --> 55:17.586
What a nut. An absolute nutjob.

904
55:18.378 --> 55:20.005
What the hell is wrong with him?

905
55:20.088 --> 55:21.089
Jeez.

906
55:48.742 --> 55:50.494
Hi, I'd like to pay the check.

907
55:51.078 --> 55:52.496
Your total is 22,000 won.

908
56:03.215 --> 56:05.592
Here. Thank you. Goodbye.

909
56:05.676 --> 56:06.677
Bye.

910
56:13.558 --> 56:15.060
Hey, Kim Sejin.

911
56:15.143 --> 56:17.145
[♪ intriguing music playing]

912
56:21.024 --> 56:22.401
Can you really promise?

913
56:22.943 --> 56:23.944
What?

914
56:24.486 --> 56:26.446
If you lose, you'll go back to Daejeon.

915
56:27.364 --> 56:29.282
Yeah, if I lose.

916
56:29.366 --> 56:32.786
But if you lose, you get lost.

917
56:35.664 --> 56:38.583
You pick the game. I don't care what we play.

918
56:39.584 --> 56:41.545
You don't care what we play?

919
56:41.628 --> 56:43.422
No, I don't.

920
56:43.505 --> 56:46.717
I'm going to beat you purely on skill.

921
56:48.677 --> 56:50.762
I never told you because I didn't want to brag,

922
56:51.471 --> 56:55.892
but my IQ is 180. That's way higher than your height.

923
56:57.227 --> 56:59.187
My IQ is 188.

924
56:59.271 --> 57:01.273
That's way higher than your height.

925
57:01.898 --> 57:02.899
That's your IQ?

926
57:02.983 --> 57:04.192
Why? Do you think I'm lying?

927
57:04.276 --> 57:07.154
An IQ of 180 or higher is extremely rare worldwide.

928
57:07.237 --> 57:09.614
Only 0.003% of people have that.

929
57:09.698 --> 57:12.200
Yeah, that number sounds about right.

930
57:13.827 --> 57:15.996
It's like rolling a six-sided die five times

931
57:16.079 --> 57:18.331
and getting the same number every time.

932
57:23.044 --> 57:24.880
0.003...

933
57:25.505 --> 57:27.299
Yeah, it's the same.

934
57:27.841 --> 57:28.842
It's...

935
57:29.760 --> 57:33.472
also the same as the odds of being dealt a royal straight flush in poker.

936
57:34.598 --> 57:36.975
Yeah, I'm good at math too.

937
57:40.437 --> 57:41.605
Do you know how to play poker?

938
57:44.566 --> 57:46.026
It's not that hard a game, is it?

939
57:47.068 --> 57:48.111
We'll play just one hand.

940
57:50.489 --> 57:52.199
And we'll keep this a secret from Minjae.

941
57:52.282 --> 57:55.619
The moment you tell him, you lose.

942
58:19.976 --> 58:21.269
[sighs]

943
58:21.353 --> 58:23.313
[♪ soft music playing]

944
58:31.863 --> 58:32.864
[grunts]

945
58:40.664 --> 58:41.748
[phone vibrating]

946
58:45.627 --> 58:46.962
Hello?

947
58:47.045 --> 58:48.046
Minjae.

948
59:13.905 --> 59:14.906
[line connects]

949
59:14.990 --> 59:16.324
-[line ringing] -[phone vibrating]

950
59:21.204 --> 59:25.000
Hey, I'm sorry, but I don't think I can come out.

951
59:27.711 --> 59:29.462
You should've given me a heads-up.

952
59:29.546 --> 59:31.756
You can't just show up because you missed me.

953
59:31.840 --> 59:34.509
I was just...

954
59:38.179 --> 59:39.890
I'll see you at school, then.

955
59:40.932 --> 59:41.933
Okay.

956
59:50.692 --> 59:52.694
[♪ gentle music playing]

957
01:00:03.914 --> 01:00:05.165
-Boo! -You scared me.

958
01:00:05.665 --> 01:00:06.666
I got you.

959
01:00:07.459 --> 01:00:08.877
I was just messing with you.

960
01:00:16.801 --> 01:00:18.678
Sorry, I kept you waiting.

961
01:01:18.363 --> 01:01:22.283
BETWEEN STEPS

962
01:01:22.367 --> 01:01:24.661
[Youjin] Professor, do you know how to play poker?

963
01:01:24.744 --> 01:01:26.287
How did you do that?

964
01:01:26.371 --> 01:01:27.664
Anyway, I'm staying here.

965
01:01:27.747 --> 01:01:29.916
I hear it's a really good opportunity.

966
01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:31.918
If you like her, you should let her go.

967
01:01:32.002 --> 01:01:33.962
I'll never give up on Youjin.

968
01:01:34.045 --> 01:01:35.463
[Youjin] Anything else besides luck?

969
01:01:35.547 --> 01:01:37.465
-[Jihoon] Mind games? -Hello.

970
01:01:37.549 --> 01:01:40.218
[Sejin] Lim Youjin, are you really going to play dirty like this?

971
01:01:40.301 --> 01:01:41.386
We're going all in.

972
01:01:41.469 --> 01:01:43.805
What the... Those punks.

973
01:01:43.888 --> 01:01:46.224
If you don't open this door before I count to three,

974
01:01:46.307 --> 01:01:48.309
you guys are going to be in serious trouble.

975
01:01:48.393 --> 01:01:49.394
Hey! [shushes]
